tests:
  unit:
    count: 19
    detail: "ui/src/FlowDetail.test.tsx REWRITTEN to the new contract — 15 tests where the shipped file had 6, fourteen of them unit; plus 4 on ui/src/components/KeyValueRow.test.tsx and 1 on Section.test.tsx from the owner's round (below). The rewrite is deliberate and is itself evidence: the old file asserted a rendered curl <pre>, a bare 'copy' label, and two body panes on the page at once — the rendered command is what W5's Tune 7 removed, and the two-pane layout is what DEC-31 replaced with one selector — so every deleted assertion maps to a design line that deleted it. Coverage: the pending panel is one mute Notice ('loading this flow…') with no identity row and no radiogroup; the identity row carries the verb through MethodLabel (toned class asserted), the status with its reason phrase as the pill's accessible name ('200 OK'), the duration through DurationText ('42 ms' with aria-label '42 milliseconds'; 1400 → '1.4 s', so the screen formats nothing), the leg radiogroup named 'leg' with request checked, and — counted, not assumed — exactly two radiogroups on the whole panel (the leg's and the pane's decode switch) plus no 'Request headers'/'Response headers' text anywhere; the URI is a 'copy uri' button whose click writes exactly the URI and confirms; the versions line reads 'HTTP/1.1 → HTTP/2.0' and drops the arrow when the response version is null; headers render in WIRE order with three set-cookie rows preserved (a keyed map would collapse them) and clicking a value writes exactly that value; a leg with no headers renders the mute Notice 'none — this leg sent no headers' while the Headers heading stays and neither segment is disabled; 'copy as curl' writes toCurl(flow), reads 'copied', reverts after CONFIRM_MS under fake timers, and the panel's text contains no curl at any point; ✕ fires onClose once; Esc from document.body fires onClose, an Esc already defaultPrevented (how Select claims its own) does not, and Esc still dismisses a panel that is only loading; and after close, document.activeElement is the element that had focus when the panel mounted. OWNER'S ROUND (real traffic buried the body under cookies and tokens): the panel never scrolls as a whole — no `overflow-auto` child of the detail root; the headers box is `overflow-auto` AND `relative` inside a Section capped at `max-h-zone-cap`; the heading names the row count ('Headers · 1'); the body Section is `flex-1 min-h-0` and the pane is `flex-1 relative` with no `max-h-` at all. A 900-character cookie renders clamped (`max-h-value-clamp`) with the whole value still the copy target, and 'more of set-cookie' under its name removes the clamp and becomes 'less of set-cookie' — jsdom lays nothing out, so a <dd> is declared 60px tall with 200px of content for that test. KeyValueRow: collapsible is off by default (a long value's cell has no class and the only button is the value); collapsible clamps an overflowing value, click still copies the WHOLE value, more expands, less collapses; a value that fits offers no toggle; a value change collapses the row again. Section: className joins the section element in both variants."
  integration:
    count: 2
    detail: "The WU's bounded contract — ONE selector governs both leg-scoped zones — in ui/src/FlowDetail.test.tsx with the real BodyViewer mounted: on open the request leg's header names are shown, the response leg's are not, the one body pane reads data-leg='request' and getBody was called for the request leg only; after clicking 'response' the header table shows content-type and not accept, there is still exactly one pane and it reads data-leg='response', getBody has been called exactly once more and for the response leg, and the flow line's textContent is byte-identical to before. In ui/src/App.test.tsx, the full keyboard path through the real FlowList: focus the listbox, ArrowDown, Enter opens the panel, Esc closes it, and document.activeElement is the listbox again — the focus-returns-to-origin receipt W5 marked blocked, now true. Three existing App tests were corrected rather than deleted: the row-click test now asserts the curl payload through the stubbed clipboard instead of a curl testid; the response-body test selects the response leg first (DEC-31: the panel opens on request); the stale-'copied' test targets the 'copy as curl' button."
  e2e:
    count: 5
    detail: "ui/e2e/specs/flows.spec.ts, against the real proxy, the real API and the real Tauri window. OWNER'S ROUND, on a new harness route /headers (three 900-character set-cookies, a bearer-sized x-token, a CSP, twelve x-trace headers over a small JSON body — the shape of the traffic that raised the complaints): 'keeps the body on screen under a wall of headers, and the window never scrolls' — more than 15 header rows rendered, document.documentElement.scrollHeight === window.innerHeight (the WebKit leak that let the window scroll four screens into nothing), the body zone at least as tall as the headers box, and the body's bottom edge inside the window; 'clamps a long header value to three lines, and more under its name shows the rest' — the cell of the row offering more has scrollHeight > clientHeight before the click and clientHeight ≥ scrollHeight (and taller) after. NEW earlier in the WU: 'the leg selector switches the headers and the body together' (request leg shows accept and not content-type; after selecting response, content-type and not accept; exactly one body-viewer; the flow line's text unchanged); 'copies a runnable curl for the request and confirms at the button' — navigator.clipboard is replaced through browser.execute with a recorder before the click, and the recorded payload is asserted to start with 'curl ', name /json and carry -H, then the button reads 'copied'; the standing 'curl as DOM text' waiver is thereby retired for this button (the OS clipboard write itself stays a manual check); and 'Esc dismisses the panel'. CORRECTED: the row-click case asserts the request leg (accept present, content-type absent, request segment aria-checked); every response-body case (brotli ×2, image, xml, truncation) goes through openResponseOf, which selects the response leg first because only the selected leg's pane exists; W8's 'shows both legs at once' case is REPLACED by the selector case per DEC-31. Hermetic: the harness's own local HTTPS origin on an ephemeral port, no public network."
verified:
  - "cd ui && pnpm test — 581 passed / 43 files, exit 0. The base (epic/redesign) is 542. Before the setup-tests.ts polyfill this branch exited 1 with one unhandled error; see below."
  - "cargo xtask ui e2e — 26 passing, 0 failing across both spec files (4 onboarding + 22 inspect) on the final run. The owner's-round cases each failed once on MY assertion, never on the product: a body-top threshold picked by hand (replaced by the claim itself — the body zone is at least as tall as the headers zone — and the headers cap tightened from 40% to 35% so it holds on a 768px window), a CSS-ancestor-plus-`button=text` selector wdio rejects (chained instead), and a class-based cell selector that picked a one-line row (the row offering more is measured instead). Earlier in the WU, the curl case took two runs — the first two runs failed only that one assertion: The first two runs each failed exactly one case, mine, in the new curl test: wdio's `button=text` selector matches direct text nodes only and CopyButton nests its label in spans (SegmentedControl's segments have direct text, which is why the idiom works there); then WebKit's getText returned 'copy as curlcopy as curl' because it includes the visibility:hidden widest-label span. Both were spec fixes; product code was not touched to make a test pass. The e2e also drove the real window to two screenshots (request leg, response leg), read and recorded in the result."
  - "cd ui && pnpm exec eslint src — clean, including the closed-vocabulary lint; the header table keeps its existing design-allow pragma for grid-cols-[auto_1fr] and no new class was minted. pnpm exec tsc --noEmit — clean."
  - "cargo fmt --check, cargo clippy --all-targets, cargo test (7 suites) — green. The only Rust change is the e2e harness's /headers route (ui/e2e/harness, outside the workspace; its pre-existing formatting is not fmt-checked and was left alone)."
  - "The page-scroll bug was reproduced and bisected in the real window before it was fixed, not guessed at: with /headers open the document's scrollHeight was 4477 against a 768px window while #root was 768; toggling styles live showed hiding the value cells → 768, the scroll container `position: relative` → 768, the aside `relative` → 768, `overflow: hidden` on the region → still 4477. So it is WebKit letting a static scroll container's overflow leak when its content is a display:contents grid, and `relative` on the headers box and the body pane is the fix; the e2e pins docScrollHeight === innerHeight."
  - "The layout was looked at as well as asserted: screenshots of the real window on the /headers flow — request leg, response leg, and after expanding a clamped cookie — are recorded in the result."
  - "The unhandled-error fix is test infrastructure and is recorded as a deviation, not smoothed over. CodeMirror measures text on the frame after mount via Range.getClientRects, which jsdom lacks, so that frame always throws. Verified in the base worktree: the identical stderr line appears and pnpm test exits 0 there, because the error lands in jsdom's virtual console while the test file is still alive. On this branch the App test that reaches the response body mounts the editor one act later (after clicking the response segment), the pending frame outlived the file, and vitest counted it as an unhandled error → exit 1. ui/src/setup-tests.ts now gives Range.prototype getClientRects/getBoundingClientRect empty implementations; verified exit 1 before, exit 0 after, and the polyfill is `??=` so a jsdom that grows them wins."
  - "The design's do-not rules were checked as code facts. No 'Request' heading over the flow line (zone B is a div; the only headings are Headers and Body, and a test asserts neither leg-named heading exists). One leg selector (a test counts every radiogroup on the panel). Nothing unbounded in row A (the URI is in B). No timer in the screen (DurationText holds a transparent placeholder when null). The command is never rendered (toCurl runs inside getPayload; unit and e2e both assert no 'curl' in the panel text). Default leg 'request' by useState, and flow.response_body is read nowhere in the file. No zebra, no eviction notice, no Notice action slot."
  - "cargo xtask verify-doc — green on the W6 plan (wu-plan), the W6 result (wu-result), the epic plan (epic-plan), web-ui.html and DEC-31 (ungoverned — link check)."
  - "cargo xtask design-scope epic/redesign HEAD — four rendering files: ui/src/FlowDetail.tsx cited to W5's run at blob 1cd046c72e9de3647211da12e31c6d6d7007d7eb; ui/src/BodyViewer.tsx, ui/src/components/KeyValueRow.tsx and ui/src/components/Section.tsx touched by the owner's round and declared design.undesigned with what each edit did (DEC-32 is the record). App.tsx, Layout.tsx and FlowList.tsx are untouched."
